64,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Toshio was executed, and no one was attacked last night. This is strange. If Toshio were the werewolf, he would have attacked.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Wait, the rules state the werewolf attacks from day 1 on. If no one died, it means the werewolf failed or something is wrong.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,2,1,talk,Minato,,No one died? That's good! I'm glad everyone is still here.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"A night of peace is unexpected. It suggests the werewolf may be playing a very cautious game, or perhaps they were hesitant.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, your relief is noted, but we must remain analytical. The lack of an attack doesn't clear anyone; it just changes the data.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Actually, if the werewolf is among us, they might have intentionally skipped an attack to appear less threatening or to sow confusion.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,2,2,talk,Minato,,"I'm sorry, I just like it when no one gets hurt. What should we do now?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I am observing the way Mizuki and Misaki are coordinating their logic. It is a strong bond, but bonds can be forged for deception.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, coordination is not deception; it is efficiency. We are trying to find the werewolf through logical deduction.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,Precisely. Jonathan's tendency to question everything without providing his own leads is starting to look like a stalling tactic.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I think Mizuki is right. Jonathan is always watching us, but he doesn't really tell us what he thinks.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I prefer to listen. However, if you find my silence suspicious, I can tell you that I find the sudden unity against me quite revealing.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"The unity is based on the fact that you provide no value to the search. Between Minato's passivity and your vagueness, one of you is the wolf.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"Minato is too transparently naive to be a strategic werewolf. Jonathan, on the other hand, is playing a psychological game.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I'll follow Mizuki. If she thinks Jonathan is the suspicious one, then I think so too.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems the quiet observer has become the target. I accept this, though I fear the village may be making a mistake in its haste.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
